WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.625 --> 00:00:01.167
[Door creaking]
- Hello?

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:01.960
Is someone there?

00:00:01.960 --> 00:00:03.211
- Uh, you're at a...

00:00:03.211 --> 00:00:05.005
darkness retreat?

00:00:05.005 --> 00:00:07.132
- What the hell is a darkness retreat?

00:00:07.132 --> 00:00:08.008
He'll never—
- Shh.

00:00:08.008 --> 00:00:09.759
- Ah, yes! A darkness retreat!

00:00:09.759 --> 00:00:12.470
And you must be my conscience.

00:00:12.470 --> 00:00:13.471
- ...Yes.

00:00:13.471 --> 00:00:14.806
I love player empowerment,

00:00:14.806 --> 00:00:16.599
but this season, Aaron got maybe

00:00:16.599 --> 00:00:17.892
TOO empowered.

00:00:17.934 --> 00:00:19.310
- So as punishment,

00:00:19.310 --> 00:00:20.645
we're brainwashing—no,

00:00:20.645 --> 00:00:22.439
strongly suggesting...

00:00:22.439 --> 00:00:24.149
that he join the Jets.

00:00:24.149 --> 00:00:24.983
No offense.

00:00:24.983 --> 00:00:26.776
- No offense is literally our problem.

00:00:26.776 --> 00:00:28.778
- Fine! I'm going to the Jets.

00:00:28.778 --> 00:00:30.321
So long as...

00:00:30.321 --> 00:00:32.657
- He wants us to sign the ghost of
Jordy Nelson,

00:00:32.657 --> 00:00:34.784
get McAfee hired at WFAN,

00:00:34.784 --> 00:00:36.369
gift him that Joe Namath jacket...

00:00:36.369 --> 00:00:38.747
- Much like my personal hero,
Scarlet Witch

00:00:38.747 --> 00:00:40.331
after she turns evil,

00:00:40.331 --> 00:00:42.667
I have eliminated all player autonomy

00:00:42.667 --> 00:00:43.293
and

00:00:43.293 --> 00:00:44.878
trapped them in a Gridiron Heights

00:00:44.878 --> 00:00:45.837
of my own making.

00:00:46.254 --> 00:00:46.880
I mean...

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:47.589
we renovated.

00:00:50.383 --> 00:00:52.010
- [Producer:] Isn't that just the same Gridiron Heights

00:00:52.010 --> 00:00:53.011
but with a monorail?

00:00:53.094 --> 00:00:54.054
- What?! No!

00:00:54.054 --> 00:00:56.431
It's a new day in Gridiron Heights.

00:00:56.431 --> 00:00:57.599
We're restructuring

00:00:57.599 --> 00:00:58.892
with some old favorites

00:00:58.892 --> 00:01:00.393
in exciting new places.

00:01:01.019 --> 00:01:01.978
- Just win, baby.

00:01:01.978 --> 00:01:03.271
The tuck rule was a fumble.

00:01:03.271 --> 00:01:05.648
Josh McDaniels is a football genius.

00:01:05.648 --> 00:01:06.858
- Oh, and you're gonna love

00:01:06.858 --> 00:01:08.359
the direction we take Derek Carr

00:01:08.359 --> 00:01:09.861
in this season.

00:01:09.861 --> 00:01:11.905
- I'm fixin' to get me some etouffee

00:01:11.905 --> 00:01:13.406
down there by the Quarter, now.

00:01:13.406 --> 00:01:15.200
- Some players were easier to

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:17.786
reprogram—I mean convince—than others!

00:01:17.786 --> 00:01:18.411
- Um, Jalen,

00:01:18.411 --> 00:01:19.496
some people were talking shit

00:01:19.496 --> 00:01:21.039
saying you'll never play for the Dolphins?

00:01:21.498 --> 00:01:22.624
- MAN! I'LL SHOW THEM.

00:01:22.624 --> 00:01:24.626
- Before long, we'll have the
Gridiron Heights

00:01:24.626 --> 00:01:25.835
I've always dreamed of,

00:01:25.835 --> 00:01:28.129
with exciting new characters!

00:01:41.935 --> 00:01:42.685
- Hmmm,

00:01:42.685 --> 00:01:44.062
I think I could mold you.

00:01:44.062 --> 00:01:46.314
- Some characters will have to be...

00:01:46.314 --> 00:01:47.065
retired.

00:01:47.065 --> 00:01:48.733
- Goodnight, Ezekiel.

00:01:48.733 --> 00:01:50.735
I loved you the very most.

00:01:50.735 --> 00:01:51.820
- But I didn't retire.

00:01:51.820 --> 00:01:52.904
You can just re-sign me!

00:01:53.154 --> 00:01:55.615
- I'm happy we got to an agreement.

00:01:55.615 --> 00:01:56.616
- Gridiron Heights:

00:01:56.616 --> 00:01:57.617
It's normal,

00:01:57.617 --> 00:01:59.410
good and free of scandal.

00:01:59.410 --> 00:02:01.538
- YOU CAN'T MAKE ME SELL!

00:02:01.538 --> 00:02:04.207
- TEAMY DISTANCING HIMSELF
FROM SNYDER!

00:02:04.207 --> 00:02:05.583
RAWR!!!
[Crashing]

00:02:06.417 --> 00:02:08.002
- This is your fault for not having an agent.

00:02:10.547 --> 00:02:12.465
- They said they're sending me to a team upstate

00:02:12.465 --> 00:02:14.551
where I'll have 
plenty of room to scramble!

00:02:14.551 --> 00:02:17.428
- They'll be back for us any minute now.

00:02:17.428 --> 00:02:18.930
Annnnnny minute.

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:20.181
- Baltimore's gonna come a-calling,

00:02:20.181 --> 00:02:21.141
just you wait.

00:02:21.599 --> 00:02:22.183
- Nexts years my year.

00:02:22.183 --> 00:02:22.767
- I could make a comeback.

00:02:22.767 --> 00:02:25.103
- Nexts years my year.
- I could make a comeback.

00:02:25.103 --> 00:02:27.021
- I'm Ryan Leaf. Get me out of here.

